      },
      "message": "fix(post): command-line post mirrors a vendor .mch like the app\n\n`post --machine <file>` handed the script the raw file, whose vendor\nkinematics tree `script_props` cannot read, so the CLI script saw no\nrotaries, spindle max, coolant codes or rates: tilted streams were\nrefused on tilthead.mch, and the spindle cap and coolant words were lost.\nThe binary now posts with `mirror(parse_mch(..))` for a vendor tree (the\napp's `machine_value_for` seam); a static-grammar file posts as written,\nand the raw-file inverted-axis and parse refusals run first, unchanged.\n\nPinned by vendor_mch_cli (tilthead tilted stream, vmc spindle cap and\nmist code, both equal to the app's program).\n\nFixes #996\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
